Group2Axioms/BaseAxiomSchema.english:
**Definition** (`BaseAxiomSchema`). The axiom instances are:
(A1) $(\varphi\dot-\psi)\dot-\varphi$;
(A2) $((\chi\dot-\varphi)\dot-(\chi\dot-\psi))\dot-(\psi\dot-\varphi)$;
(A3) $(\varphi\dot-(\varphi\dot-\psi))\dot-(\psi\dot-(\psi\dot-\varphi))$;
(A4) $(\varphi\dot-\psi)\dot-(\neg\psi\dot-\neg\varphi)$;
(A5) $\tfrac12\varphi\dot-(\varphi\dot-\tfrac12\varphi)$;
(A6) $(\varphi\dot-\tfrac12\varphi)\dot-\tfrac12\varphi$;
(A7) $(\sup_x\psi\dot-\sup_x\varphi)\dot-\sup_x(\psi\dot-\varphi)$;
(A8) $\varphi[t/x]\dot-\sup_x\varphi$, provided the substitution is correct;
(A9) $\sup_x\varphi\dot-\varphi$, provided $x\notin\mathrm{FV}(\varphi)$.

LanguageAndSemantics/MetricPreStructure.english:
**Definition** (`MetricPreStructure`). For a signature with a metric, a metric pre-structure is a pre-structure in which, writing $d(x,y)$ for the value of the metric symbol at $(x,y)$:
1. $d(a,a)=0$, $d(a,b)=d(b,a)$ and $d(a,c)\le d(a,b)+d(b,c)$ (with values in $[0,1]$ inherited from the pre-structure);
2. for each function symbol $f$, place $i$ and $\epsilon\in(0,1]$: if $d(c,e)<\delta_{f,i}(\epsilon)$ then $d(f(v[i\mapsto c]),f(v[i\mapsto e]))\le\epsilon$ for every tuple $v$;
3. for each relation symbol $P$, place $i$ and $\epsilon\in(0,1]$: if $d(c,e)<\delta_{P,i}(\epsilon)$ then $P(v[i\mapsto c])\dot-P(v[i\mapsto e])\le\epsilon$.
